# Replay corpus entry: envelope-full (replay-command format v1).
#
# The first committed replay in the production replay-command format
# (src/CommandoWar.Sim/ReplaySerialisation.fs, TASK-025 / backlog B-045). It
# carries a full accepted-command envelope the legacy .cwlog cannot express:
# a three-recipient MoveTo (agents 3, 4, 5), Urgency = immediate,
# RiskTolerance = aggressive, issued on tick 1 and delivered on tick 2.
#
# Initial state: the shared spike fixture (Setup.sixAgentWorld, 32 x 32,
# seed 20260902) — resolved by name from Corpus.all, not serialised.
#
# canonical 7 and every hash below were re-pinned by TASK-034 (backlog B-022,
# partial; Canonical.FormatVersion 6 -> 7, WorldState.HostileTacticalKnowledge
# added). The spike fixture has zero enemy deployments, so the new section is
# empty at every checkpoint: the 24 ticks and 78 domain events are unchanged,
# a byte-layout-only re-pin. Prior re-pin: TASK-033 (Canonical.FormatVersion
# 5 -> 6, AgentState.SuppressionBand / .Stress added).
